course: dictionary
lesson: 13721
title: Words for people who teach skills
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: An instructor is a person who teaches a practical skill or sport, such as driving, swimming, skiing or climbing. You learn by doing, not just by reading about it. The context helps you: «My swimming instructor helped me float on my back.» Swimming and float tell you the instructor is a teacher in the pool.
explain: Look at the word inside instructor: instruct means to teach. An instructor is the person who does the teaching. Instructors work in many places. A driving instructor teaches you on the road, a ski instructor teaches you on the snow, and a fitness instructor leads you through exercise at the gym.
explain: «The ski instructor showed us how to turn on the slope.» Ask yourself: what does this person teach? The word slope and the word ski give the clue. Then try your meaning in the sentence. A person who teaches a skill fits, so your meaning is right.
fact: An instructor is a person who teaches a practical skill or sport.
fact: Examples: driving instructor, swimming instructor, ski instructor, fitness instructor.
fact: Instructor comes from the word instruct, which means to teach.
fact: Context clues such as swimming, skiing or driving tell you what an instructor teaches.
exercise: «My swimming instructor helped me float on my back.» What is an instructor? | *A person who teaches a practical skill, such as swimming | A large pool with a glass roof | A bag for carrying swimming clothes | A type of fish found in rivers
exercise: Which phrase means a person who teaches you to drive? | *driving instructor | driving test | car park | motorway
exercise: «The ski instructor showed us how to turn on the slope.» Find and copy one word that tells you what the instructor teaches. | slope | turn | showed | *ski
test: «The fitness instructor counted our press-ups at the gym.» What does instructor mean here? | *A person who leads and teaches exercise | A person who cleans the gym floor | A customer who pays to join the gym | A machine that counts reps
test: Which sentence uses instructor correctly? | The instructor was a red bus that went to school. | *Dad is my driving instructor, and he teaches me to change gear. | The instructor of the cake was very tasty at breakfast. | I put the instructor on my bike to keep it dry.
exam: What does an instructor teach? | Only dates from history | *A practical skill or sport, such as swimming or skiing | Only how to bake bread at home | Only numbers and sums
